---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import CopyableCode from "../../components/CopyableCode.astro";
import { InsetText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-astro";
---

<ToolingLayout title="Set up Pi" currentPath="/tooling/pi">
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Set up Pi</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Pi is a terminal-based coding agent. If you connect it to the AI Gateway it
    will give you access to any{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/models">
      available AI model
    </a>{" "}
    (for example, Claude or Gemini).
  </p>

  <figure class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-6">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/gateway-diagram-pi.svg"
      alt="Diagram showing Pi running in the terminal, connecting to the AI Gateway, which provides access to Claude, Gemini, GPT and other AI models."
      class="govuk-!-width-full"
    />
  </figure>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Before you start, make sure you have{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
      your AI Gateway key
    </a>
    . Then, to set up Pi, you need to:
  </p>
  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#use-admin-permissions">
        Use admin permissions
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-pi">
        Install Pi and add your AI Gateway key
      </a>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These steps work for most setups. If you run into issues you can't resolve,
    contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel on i.AI Slack.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="use-admin-permissions">
    Use admin permissions
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You need (temporary) admin permissions to install software on your Mac.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Select the padlock icon (<strong>Local Admin Management</strong>) on the
      top menu bar.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Install an app</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>Start session</strong>, and enter your laptop password.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>OK</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These permissions last for 10 minutes. Select the padlock to request more
    time.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-pi">
    Install Pi and add your AI Gateway key
  </h2>

  <InsetText>
    Requires macOS and Node 22.19.0 or newer (
    <code class="app-code">node -v</code> to check).
  </InsetText>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To install Pi, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="curl -fsSL https://pi.dev/install.sh | sh" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To install the LiteLLM extension, run:
      <CopyableCode code="pi install npm:pi-provider-litellm" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m" id="pi-add-your-key">
    Add or renew your key
  </h3>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Copy your AI Gateway key (
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
        how to get your key
      </a>
      ).
    </li>
    <li>
      To start Pi, in Terminal, run <code class="app-code">pi</code> from any
      project directory, then log in:
      <CopyableCode code="/login litellm" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Sign in with an API key</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Enter:
      <CopyableCode code="https://llm-gateway.i.ai.gov.uk" />
    </li>
    <li>Paste your AI Gateway key.</li>
    <li>
      To confirm it worked, run:
      <CopyableCode code="/model" />
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Gateway models appear as{" "}
        <code class="app-code">litellm/&lt;model-name&gt;</code>.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Nothing to maintain after that: opening <code class="app-code">/model</code>{" "}
    refreshes the model list in the background, and{" "}
    <code class="app-code">pi update --models</code> forces it. See the{" "}
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://pi.dev/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Pi documentation
    </a>{" "}
    for troubleshooting (including TLS/certificate errors on networks that
    intercept HTTPS) and how to disable the MCP tools and skills the extension
    enables by default.
  </p>

  <InsetText>
    To renew an expired key, repeat the{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="#pi-add-your-key">
      Add your key
    </a>{" "}
    steps above with your new key.
  </InsetText>
</ToolingLayout>
